    {
      "source": "hn",
      "title": "Show HN: Fast deterministic natural language search for OpenStreetMap data",
      "url": "https://hippomaps.ch/?q=cafes+by+the+Limmat+100+m+from+the+lake+in+zurich#map=15.02/47.36708/8.54935",
      "author": "vihren",
      "external_id": "50561199",
      "summary": null,
      "why_read": null,
      "authors": [],
      "category": null,
      "published": "2026-11-19T15:16:02Z",
      "score": 79,
      "comments": 24,
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50561199",
      "snippet": "I want to show you HippoMaps. It is a fully featured map and navigation app built on OpenStreetMap with a custom Overpass API engine for really fast search of POIs, areas and ways.<p>My aim with HippoMaps is to get to a level where I don&#x27;t need Google Maps anymore. The biggest hurdle IMHO with OSM based apps is the lack of nice and fast search (where GMaps excels at). To get there I started working on a deterministic (as in no LLMs used) parser of queries that translates them to the Overpass QL.<p>Search queries are split into tokens and the algorithm tries to guess &quot;what&quot; you want to search and &quot;where&quot;. The former comes from a word list (known brands, sports, OSM tags) and the latter from the geocoder service (Photon).<p>You can get quite creative like &quot;cafes in Zurich by the Limmat&quot;, &quot;peaks over 4000 m in Valais&quot;, &quot;pharmacies open now i",
      "links": []
    },
